## Workflow gotchas learned
- `ar0521` is `=m`. Any `ar0521.c` change needs `bitbake karo-image-minimal` and a **rootfs** reflash; bootfs alone only carries `Image` + dtb.
- Modules are built by `do_compile_kernelmodules`, not `do_compile`.
- Before every flash, check the **deploy-dir symlink target timestamp** (`ls -la tmp/deploy/images/qsxp-ml81/*.ext4`), not the mtime of the copy. A stale bootfs in `~/uuu-flash` caused a false "regression" once.
- Check builds without flashing: `strings`/`nm` on `.../build/drivers/media/i2c/ar0521.o`, and on target `strings /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/kernel/drivers/media/i2c/ar0521.ko`.
- Generate patches with `diff -u` from pristine plus edited copies. Hand-edited hunk headers silently dropped lines once.
- `/tmp` on the build VM is wiped on reboot; keep working files elsewhere.
- Board is BusyBox: no `timeout`, no `dmesg -C` (use `dmesg -c`), no `lsblk`/`findmnt`.
- A failed or removed ar0521 probe leaves the sensor held in reset, so it vanishes from `i2cdetect`. Sysfs GPIO exports don't survive reboot, and a leftover export blocks the driver's `gpiod_get`.
- U-Boot `fdt set` of a new property needs `fdt resize` first (FDT_ERR_NOSPACE). Running `bootcmd_mmc` again reloads the DTB and discards edits.
